WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:08.225 line:0 align:center
Any dash can open another dash with a button. These linked dashes are called sub dashes.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.225 line:0 align:center
Here, these two dock buttons open other dashes.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.875 line:0 align:center
To see how they connect, open Sub dashes.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.925 line:0 align:center
It's the map of your dashes. The arrows show which dash opens which.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.425 line:0 align:center
Add a button that opens another dash, and a new arrow appears.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.025 line:0 align:center
New sub dash creates a new dash.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.075 line:0 align:center
Edit this dash opens the selected dash in Layout.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.300 line:0 align:center
Each dash can also have its own dock.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.475 line:0 align:center
That's the dock: the toolbar on the side of the dash.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:55.200 line:0 align:center
With many dashes, keeping every dock consistent takes work. Each one needs a way back, for example.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:02.525 line:0 align:center
Instead, select the main dash and turn on Use its dock on every dash.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:07.025 line:0 align:center
That dock then shows on all your dashes.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.775 line:0 align:center
The other docks are not deleted, only hidden. They come back when you turn this off.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.525 line:0 align:center
You can pick any dash as the source of the shared dock.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.250 line:0 align:center
Every panel has a short note that explains its options. Read it first: most answers are there.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:29.150 line:0 align:center
Back on the main dash, Links shows where each dash is opened from.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:36.550 line:0 align:center
Click one to jump straight to it. Handy when you have many dashes.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.525 line:0 align:center
The Music page is built in, and it can't be edited.

00:01:44.075 --> 00:01:47.250 line:0 align:center
It shows the app that's playing music on your phone.

00:01:50.325 --> 00:01:53.250 line:0 align:center
And it opens from the music button on the dock.

00:01:55.575 --> 00:01:59.975 line:0 align:center
Under This sub dash, you can rename, duplicate or delete a dash.

00:02:01.275 --> 00:02:04.275 line:0 align:center
And under Icon, you can change its icon.

00:02:05.025 --> 00:02:08.650 line:0 align:center
Click Edit this dash, and you're back in Layout to change it.

00:02:10.175 --> 00:02:12.850 line:0 align:center
It works the same for every sub dash.

00:02:13.275 --> 00:02:19.475 line:0 align:center
This dash's own dock is only a rough draft. That's fine: every dash shows the main dock.

00:02:20.125 --> 00:02:24.475 line:0 align:center
Here's an example. This widget opens a sub dash called Waze.

00:02:26.075 --> 00:02:28.900 line:0 align:center
That dash holds just one big app card.

00:02:30.825 --> 00:02:34.075 line:0 align:center
So Waze fills the screen, right next to the dock.
